[h2]The Enslaver of Souls and the pets you summon from his soul now carry the black shroud[/h2]
[list]
[*]The Enslaver's own summoned demons have always smoked. He did not, and neither did the versions of him you summon from his soul. The previous update said it had fixed that. It had not, and this note is the correction: the effect was written into monster skill slots [b]the engine does not read[/b].
[*]The game's monster skill manager declares slots 1 through 17 and nothing above them. Across all 74,013 base-game records, no monster and no pet ever uses a higher slot. The last update parked the shroud at slot 19 on the boss and slot 18 on all three summoned tiers, so four fields were written and none of them were ever loaded. Everything built on top of them was correct and unreachable.
[*]The shroud now rides the two always-on channels that template actually declares: the skill cast once at spawn, so it is on from the first frame and never waits on combat AI, and the self-buff channel the creature's own controller re-applies whenever possible. Both are ordinary skill fields, which is the only class this game's pet records tolerate.
[/list]

[h2]The whole household is now checked, not just half of it[/h2]
[list]
[*]The earlier check only ever covered the boss and the three pet tiers his soul summons. It never looked at the marauders he raises, nor at the marauders that a summoned Enslaver raises in turn. Those were smoking by luck, because their rig carries the effect compiled into the mesh, and a mesh swap could have removed that silently at any time.
[*]The build now walks the entire family (boss, escorts, summoned tiers, and the pets those pets raise) and refuses to build unless every member carries the shroud by one of two proven routes: compiled into its rig, or present in both always-on channels. On this build that resolves to eight family members, four covered by their mesh and four by the fields.
[/list]

[h2]Your existing souls already in the stash are fine[/h2]
[list]
[*]This effect lives on the pet records, which the game resolves from the database at the moment the summon fires. It is not baked into the soul item when you pick it up, the way item stats are. So the Enslaver souls already in your stash pick this up with no re-drop and no new character. A full restart to reload the database is enough.
[/list]

[i]Scope, measured rather than asserted: this update changes [b]four records[/b] and sixteen fields, all of them on the Enslaver and his three summoned tiers. No records were added or removed, nothing else in 51,331 records moved, and no item, drop rate, chest, quest, area or map data changed. The world map, quest archive, text archive and creature archive are byte for byte identical to the previous update.[/i]

[i]Not yet confirmed in play: this is the fourth attempt at this one request and the first three were record-level claims that were wrong in game. What is proved here is that the shroud now sits on channels the engine declares and reads, and that the gate reproduces the old bug as an artifact fact. What is not proved is how it looks on screen.[/i]

